  3.2     Measure of Inﬂuence: Time-Balanced Network Centrality
                     号




  3.2.1   Model of Rescaled PageRank
            信




     For a social network, it’s natural to gauge the inﬂuence of nodes by methods includ-
  ing centrality, Pagerank etc. However, traditional PageRank will meet several prob-
    微




  lems in this question: 1. it ignores the time structure of the network, which could pro-
  duce unrealistic features[4]; 2. the redistribution of PageRank is temporally strongly
  biased towards old nodes[5], which makes the PageRank scores of new nodes from 10s
    1 All these phonomenon help explain the plausibility of Assumption 2, as there are very few young-

  sters affect older generations, it won’t make a big difference to the result.
