      By the property of small-world, we consider the cosine similarity of nodes by its
  geodesic distance in the network. We don’t think for nodes whose distance above 5 still
  have similarities as it’s way bigger than the average distance even in the undirected
  network. So with geodesic distance below 6, we separate the space between [0, π2 ]
  into 6 parts to get an "expected similarity". By minimizing the squared error between
  similarity and "expected similarity", we are able to ﬁgure out the optimized weight
微信号：MATHmodels
  vector by stochastic gradient descent[8].
